---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
import { url } from '../utils/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description={`Terms governing the use of the ${siteConfig.name} website.`}
>
  <section class="border-b border-line bg-surface">
    <div class="shell py-8 sm:py-10">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Terms' }]} />
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-display-2">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9rem] text-ink-subtle">Last updated: September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="shell prose-body">
      <h2>What the listings on this site are, and are not</h2>
      <p>
        Project details — unit counts, built-up areas, configurations, possession dates, amenities
        and specifications — are reproduced as published by the developer. We do not independently
        verify them, and they can change without notice. Nothing on this site is an offer, and no
        listing is a representation that a specific unit is available.
      </p>
      <p>
        Prices are shared on request; where a page says "price on request" it is because no price
        has been published, not because one is being withheld. Area figures for individual units,
        where absent, are absent for the same reason. Some project images are artist's impressions
        rather than photographs of the completed building. Area price ranges and travel times shown
        on location pages are indicative orientation only and should not be relied on as market data.
      </p>

      <h2>No advice, no guarantees</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this website is financial, legal, tax or investment advice. We do not guarantee any
        rate of return, rate of appreciation, rental yield, or resale value on any property. Where this
        site discusses general factors affecting the Hyderabad property market, that discussion is
        background — not a forecast, and not a recommendation to buy.
      </p>

      <h2>Verify everything independently</h2>
      <p>
        Before committing to any transaction you should independently verify title, encumbrance,
        layout and building approvals, RERA registration, occupancy certificate, measurements, and all
        costs, using your own lawyer and your own advisers. Figures such as the indicative stamp duty
        and registration estimates shown on listing pages are planning aids computed from published
        rates; the amount actually payable depends on the document and the property and may differ.
      </p>

      <h2>The property assistant</h2>
      <p>
        The assistant on this site is a scripted demonstration. It follows a fixed set of questions and
        matches against the same listing data as the rest of the site. It is not an artificial
        intelligence system, it does not have access to live inventory, and its suggestions carry no
        more weight than the listing data behind them.
      </p>

      <h2>The EMI calculator</h2>
      <p>
        The calculator applies the standard reducing-balance formula to the numbers you enter. It is an
        estimate for planning. Actual loan terms, eligibility, fees and the EMI quoted to you are
        determined by your lender.
      </p>

      <h2>External links and images</h2>
      <p>
        We link to third-party sites, including WhatsApp, Instagram and Facebook, and we are not
        responsible for their content or their terms. Photographs are used under the licences recorded
        on the <a href={url('/credits')}>image credits page</a>; copyright remains with the respective
        authors.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        We make no commitment that this site will be available uninterrupted or free of errors, and we
        may change or remove any content without notice.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of India, with courts at Hyderabad, Telangana having
        jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Anything unclear here can be raised with us directly — see the{' '}
        <a href={url('/contact')}>contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
